I haven't played 3.0 yet (just too doggone much to compile and port to VMS,
and I've got a working 2.3 here anyway) but the Tourist was definitely my
class of choice back in the days when I played a lot of Hack.

I would usually re-roll the character until I got 2 or 3 cans of spinach,
which cured my strength problems right away.  Then (assuming the spinach
did the trick) I was pretty much on my way down to meet the wiz.  Having
all of the extra food does wonders for training your dog (just toss out
a dart, wait for him to bring it back, and toss him tripe ... repeat
once or twice).  Furthermore, the camera's flash is an incredibly effective
weapon.

In fact, I thought the tourist was so easy to play that I eventually 
started to play the other "harder" classes out of boredom...

My contribution to my version of 2.3 was the addition of "QUARRY" rooms ...
You step into one and it looks something like:

 #########
 #------- 
##+)`.`.+ 
##|))`).| 
#d@)`.))+ 
  ------- 

There are occasionally things (usually cheap gems, sometimes other stuff)
underneath the boulders.  The message you get when entering the room is:

	"It looks rather rocky in here."

I thought it was kind of cute ... it's quite a challenge, sometimes, to try
and look under all of the boulders without getting stuck.

